    "question": "Carmen needs $7 more to have twice the amount of money that Jethro has. Meanwhile, Patricia has $60, which is 3 times as much as Jethro. What is the sum of all their money?",
    "gold": "113",
    "answer": "Jethro has 60/3 = $<<60/3=20>>20.\nTwice of what Jethro has is $20 x 2 = $40\nCarmen has $40 - 7 = $<<40-7=33>>33\nThe sum of all their money is $60 + $20 + $33 = $<<60+20+33=113>>113\n#### 113"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the amounts of money that Carmen, Jethro, and Patricia have, and then find the sum of their money.\n\nFirst, let's define the variables:\n- Let \\( J \\) be the amount of money Jethro has.\n- Let \\( C \\) be the amount of money Carmen has.\n- Let \\( P \\) be the amount of money Patricia has.\n\nFrom the problem, we know:\n1. Patricia has $60, which is 3 times as much as Jethro. Therefore, we can write:\n   \\[\n   P = 3J\n   \\]\n   Since \\( P = 60 \\), we can substitute to find \\( J \\):\n   \\[\n   60 = 3J \\implies J = \\frac{60}{3} = 20\n   \\]\n   So, Jethro has $20.\n\n2. Carmen needs $7 more to have twice the amount of money that Jethro has. Therefore, we can write:\n   \\[\n   C + 7 = 2J\n   \\]\n   Since \\( J = 20 \\), we can substitute to find \\( C \\):\n   \\[\n   C + 7 = 2 \\times 20 \\implies C + 7 = 40 \\implies C = 40 - 7 = 33\n   \\]\n   So, Carmen has $33.\n\nNow, we know the amounts of money each person has:\n- Jethro has $20.\n- Carmen has $33.\n- Patricia has $60.\n\nThe sum of their money is:\n\\[\n20 + 33 + 60 = 113\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all their money is \\(\\boxed{113}\\).",
